# Plan Adherence

Before implementing any feature, creating any file, or adding any dependency, verify it
traces to the approved product plan.

[Corpus: product] [Corpus: system-spec] [Corpus: deps]

## Feature Scope

All implementation work must map to an approved feature in `docs/feature-list.md`
(ChatRAG / Data Management / cross-cutting Fn — currently through **F77**). Cite the
feature section (e.g. `[Corpus: feature-list.md §F75]`).

Do **not** use leftover Job-template / RFantibody F1–F9 mappings (RFdiffusion,
ProteinMPNN, RF2). Those are not Vecinita product features.

If work does not map to an approved `feature-list.md` Fn, raise `[Scope Drift]` via
AskQuestion:
- Cite the code or file being created
- Explain which feature it was intended for
- First option: "Map to feature FN — here's why..."
- Last option: "Let me explain / provide more context"

### Out of Scope (do not implement without a new Fn + decision)

- Live production corpus mutation / FT promote without AskQuestion
  ([no-live-prod-corpus-push.mdc](no-live-prod-corpus-push.mdc))
- Antibody / RFantibody pipeline stages, PyRosetta, or Job-template `src/` layout
- Inventing Fn for exploratory mocks (e.g. community maps HTML) without intake
- Paid third-party LLM/embed APIs as the default path (spec H6)

## Component Verification

New files must map to an approved surface from `docs/spec.md` / `docs/architecture.md`:

| Surface | Expected location |
|---------|-------------------|
| ChatRAG API | `apps/chat-rag-backend/` |
| ChatRAG UI | `apps/chat-rag-frontend/` |
| Data management ASGI / workers | `apps/data-management-backend/` |
| Admin UI | `apps/data-management-frontend/` |
| Internal write API | `apps/internal-write-api/` |
| Migrations / seeds | `apps/database/` |
| Shared libraries | `packages/{rag,ingest,embedding-client,llm-client,tagging,eval,shared-schemas,frontend-*}/` |
| Modal apps | `infra/modal/` (`embedding_app`, `data_management_app`, `llm_app`, `llm_playground_app`, `finetune_app`) |
| DO app specs | `infra/do/*.yaml` (SECRET placeholders only) |
| Tests | `tests/` (+ colocated frontend `*.test.tsx`) |

Files outside these locations require justification. Raise `[Scope Drift]` if a new
deployable or package is introduced without a corpus/ADR update.

## Dependency Verification

Before adding any new dependency, check `docs/dependency-inventory.md`. If the dependency
is not listed:
1. Raise `[Decision]` with a recommendation
2. On approval, back-add to `docs/dependency-inventory.md`
3. Record the decision in `docs/decisions/evolve-decisions.md` (or the active session log)
